  "officialTimeMinutes": 27,
  "bodyHtml": "<p>While touring the <span class=\"data\">sìì jaŋgidḕ</span> (\"school\"), you attempt to learn a few words of Nizaa, with the help of a few trusty flashcards. Unfortunately, someone failed to print the flashcards double-sided! Your job is to match the Nizaa (left) and English (right) back together.</p>\n<div class=\"table-scroll\">\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th>Nizaa</th><th>English</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>1. <span class=\"data\">ɓeè</span></td><td>A. <em>Anthocleista vogelii</em></td></tr>\n<tr><td>2. <span class=\"data\">ɓeè nim</span></td><td>B. calabash</td></tr>\n<tr><td>3. <span class=\"data\">ɓòw</span></td><td>C. carpenter</td></tr>\n<tr><td>4. <span class=\"data\">ɓòw-ŋwiiŋ</span></td><td>D. cup (for drinking water)</td></tr>\n<tr><td>5. <span class=\"data\">ɓʉʉ</span></td><td>E. dog</td></tr>\n<tr><td>6. <span class=\"data\">cam fwɛ̀ɛŋ</span></td><td>F. duck</td></tr>\n<tr><td>7. <span class=\"data\">cam-ŋwiiŋ</span></td><td>G. fingernail</td></tr>\n<tr><td>8. <span class=\"data\">cún fwɛ̀ɛŋ</span></td><td>H. hairdresser</td></tr>\n<tr><td>9. <span class=\"data\">cún nim</span></td><td>I. head</td></tr>\n<tr><td>10. <span class=\"data\">ɗɔ́ɔŋ</span></td><td>J. hunter</td></tr>\n<tr><td>11. <span class=\"data\">ɗɔ́ɔŋ nim</span></td><td>K. little finger</td></tr>\n<tr><td>12. <span class=\"data\">hodḕ ɗɔ́ɔŋ</span></td><td>L. puppy</td></tr>\n<tr><td>13. <span class=\"data\">nìì cún</span></td><td>M. roof</td></tr>\n<tr><td>14. <span class=\"data\">nìì gírcí ɓʉʉ</span></td><td>N. sauce</td></tr>\n<tr><td>15. <span class=\"data\">nìì kwɛ́ɛŋ</span></td><td>O. sauce spoon</td></tr>\n<tr><td>16. <span class=\"data\">nim</span></td><td>P. soup</td></tr>\n<tr><td>17. <span class=\"data\">nim ɓʉʉ</span></td><td>Q. source of water</td></tr>\n<tr><td>18. <span class=\"data\">sìì ɓʉʉ</span></td><td>R. teardrop</td></tr>\n<tr><td>19. <span class=\"data\">sìŋw kwɛ́ɛŋ</span></td><td>S. tree bark</td></tr>\n<tr><td>20. <span class=\"data\">sìŋw nim</span></td><td>T. water</td></tr>\n<tr><td>21. <span class=\"data\">yír nim</span></td><td>U. wild bird</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n</div>\n<p><em>Notes:</em> Nizaa is spoken by about 10,000 people in Cameroon. <em>Anthocleista vogelii</em> is a species of tree that thrives in the rainforest. A <em>calabash</em> is a gourd (a type of hard-shelled fruit, similar to a pumpkin) that is often hollowed out and dried for use as a container. Pronunciation is not relevant for solving this problem, but <span class=\"data\">ɓ</span>, <span class=\"data\">ŋ</span>, and <span class=\"data\">ɗ</span> are consonants; <span class=\"data\">ʉ</span>, <span class=\"data\">ɛ</span>, and <span class=\"data\">ɔ</span> are vowels; and marks above vowels indicate tone—the pitch used when pronouncing a vowel.</p>\n<p><strong>F1.</strong> Indicate which English translations go with which Nizaa words and phrases.</p>\n<p><strong>F2.</strong> Translate into Nizaa: a. <em>bush</em>, b. <em>hut</em>, c. <em>to read</em>, d. <em>to shave</em>.</p>",
