  "hints": [
    {
      "tier": 1,
      "text": "Five Nizaa entries are single words that also turn up inside longer entries: ɓeè, ɓòw, ɓʉʉ, ɗɔ́ɔŋ and nim. Any English gloss you assign to one of those single words has to keep making sense in every longer phrase that contains it.",
      "xpCost": 2
    },
    {
      "tier": 2,
      "text": "Look at the English column as a set of recipes rather than a list of words. Several glosses are really \"a small X\" or \"the outer covering of X\" or \"a person who does X\" or \"the X of water\". Nizaa builds those same meanings by putting two ordinary words side by side, so a repeated Nizaa element should line up with a repeated English idea.",
      "xpCost": 3
